# Practical: Develop Application to Consume Google Map RESTful Web Service

## Step 1: Create a New Web Application

1. Open **NetBeans IDE** and select **New Project**.
2. Choose **Java Web → Web Application** and click **Next**.
3. Enter the **Project Name: Practical4** and select the project location.
4. Select **Server: GlassFish Server 4.1**.
5. Select **Java EE Version: Java EE 7 Web**.
6. Set the **Context Path: /Practical4**.
7. Click **Finish** (no frameworks required).

---

# Step 2: Create the Input Page (input.jsp)

1. Right-click the project **Practical4**.
2. Select **New → JSP**.
3. Enter the **File Name: input** and click **Finish**.

### input.jsp

```html
<html>
<body>

<h2>Google Map Location Viewer</h2>

<form action="index.jsp">

Enter Latitude:
<input type="text" name="t1"/>

<br><br>

Enter Longitude:
<input type="text" name="t2"/>

<br><br>

<input type="submit" value="Show"/>

</form>

</body>
</html>
```

---

# Step 3: Obtain a Google API Key

1. Open the **Google APIs Console** in your browser.
2. Sign in with your **Google account**.
3. Click **Create Project** and enter a name (for example **DemoProject**).
4. Open **API Library**.
5. Search for **Maps JavaScript API**.
6. Click **Enable**.
7. Go to the **Credentials** tab.
8. Click **+ Create Credentials → API Key**.
9. Copy the generated **API Key** for use in your program.

---

# Step 4: Create the Display Page (index.jsp)

1. Right-click the project.
2. Select **New → JSP**.
3. Enter the **File Name: index** and click **Finish**.

### index.jsp

```jsp
<%

double lati = Double.parseDouble(request.getParameter("t1"));
double longi = Double.parseDouble(request.getParameter("t2"));

%>

<html>
<head>

<style>
#map {
height: 500px;
width: 100%;
}
</style>

<script>

function initMap() {

var location = {lat: <%=lati%>, lng: <%=longi%>};

var map = new google.maps.Map(document.getElementById("map"), {
zoom: 10,
center: location
});

var marker = new google.maps.Marker({
position: location,
map: map
});

}

</script>

</head>

<body>

<h2>Google Map Location</h2>

<div id="map"></div>

<script async defer
src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=YOUR_API_KEY&callback=initMap">
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

Replace **YOUR_API_KEY** with the **actual Google API key**.

---

# Step 5: Run and Test the Application

1. Right-click the project **Practical4**.
2. Select **Deploy**.
3. Right-click **input.jsp** and select **Run File**.
4. The browser will open the input page.
5. Enter values such as:

```
Latitude: 19.0260
Longitude: 72.8553
```

6. Click **Show**.

The Google Map will open and **display a marker at the entered location**.

---

# Result

The web application successfully consumed **Google Maps RESTful Web Service** using latitude and longitude values and displayed the specified location on the Google Map.
